FitHub Phase 2 defect and retest register
Date: 2026-09-17

DEF-001 — Attendance scanner submit did not invoke check-in
- Original result: clicking “Validate and check in QR” produced no request and no attendance row.
- Cause: a plain standalone form used ngSubmit without the required form directive/import.
- Affected file: frontend/fithub-web/src/app/features/attendance/scanner/scanner-page.html
- Fix: use the native submit event, invoke scan(), and prevent the browser’s default submit.
- Retest: PASS. Check-in accepted; token reuse rejected; attendance persisted.

DEF-002 — Trainer assignment form did not invoke assignment
- Original result: Administrator selection and submit produced no assignment.
- Cause: the same plain-form ngSubmit wiring problem.
- Affected file: frontend/fithub-web/src/app/features/administration/trainers/trainer-assignment-page.html
- Fix: use the native submit event and prevent default submission.
- Retest: PASS. Tariq→Elena assignment persisted and appeared for the Trainer.

DEF-003 — Successful scanner check-in also displayed a required-field error
- Original result: after success, clearing the text value left the control touched, so success and validation error appeared together.
- Cause: setValue('') did not reset the control interaction state.
- Affected file: frontend/fithub-web/src/app/features/attendance/scanner/scanner-page.ts
- Fix: reset('') after successful check-in.
- Retest: production build PASS; final browser-only visual retest remains outstanding.

DEF-004 — Connected equipment clearance emits contradictory events
- Original result: both shared Members leaving produced countdown start, backend-unavailable, immediate enter and cancellation events; automatic release did not complete.
- Likely affected area: equipment simulation sensor-zone transition/reconciliation and connected event submission.
- Status: OPEN. Not changed in this testing task because it requires a focused simulation fix.

DEF-005 — Workout sets have no dedicated rest-time field
- Original result: 90-second rest had to be written in exercise notes.
- Affected area: workout set DTO, domain persistence and Angular session form.
- Status: OPEN.

DEF-006 — Notification preferences are absent
- Original result: notifications and deduplication exist, but no preference persistence or interface exists.
- Affected area: notification domain/API/frontend.
- Status: OPEN.

GAP-001 — Registration consent is absent from the public registration workflow.
GAP-002 — Forgot-password does not deliver a single-use reset link; the generated token is discarded.
